{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1887 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "9d9b9ae0ac485b38138004b323604bee3a60e64f358ad84236aa11b77d298961" :edb/db-before-t 1886 :edb/db-after-t 1887 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535199 50 #inst "2026-10-08T19:21:19.499Z" 13194139535199 true] [17592186119701 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337084 13194139535199 true] [17592186119771 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337091 13194139535199 true] [17592186119771 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337098 13194139535199 true] [17592186119772 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337077 13194139535199 true] [17592186120440 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535199 true] [17592186120440 1100 "Suppose $B$ is a $2 \\cdot 2$ matrix and $det(B) =-2$. What is the value of $det(3B)$?" 13194139535199 false] [17592186120440 1100 "Suppose $B$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $det(B)=-2.$ What is the value of $det(3B)?$" 13194139535199 true] [17592186120440 1145 "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot B)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=3$ and $n=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(3B) & ={3}^{2}\\cdot det(B) \\\\  & =9\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337077 1017 #edb/ref 17592186337078 13194139535199 true] [17592186337077 1089 "q-130739" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337077 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535199 true] [17592186337077 1100 "Suppose $Y$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $det(Y)=2.$ What is the value of $det(-4Y)?$" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337077 1113 #uuid "8b833eb4-9e05-5944-8297-af141a86129b" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337077 1145 "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot Y)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(Y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=-4$ and $n=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(-4Y) & =(-4)^{3}\\cdot det(Y) \\\\  & =-64\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-128.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337078 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337079 13194139535199 true] [17592186337078 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337080 13194139535199 true] [17592186337078 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337081 13194139535199 true] [17592186337078 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337082 13194139535199 true] [17592186337078 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337083 13194139535199 true] [17592186337078 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535199 true] [17592186337078 1041 "selection" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337078 1104 #edb/ref 17592186337080 13194139535199 true] [17592186337078 1110 #uuid "0886aaa0-7d4a-5c70-b7ea-32b77b2b39a8" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337079 1034 "-88" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337079 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535199 true] [17592186337079 1111 #uuid "9708b244-f64c-5021-bea5-de40ca1711ae" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337080 1034 "-128" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337080 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535199 true] [17592186337080 1111 #uuid "32452624-c669-5a2a-af81-9a45d8922ef4" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337081 1034 "-64" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337081 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535199 true] [17592186337081 1111 #uuid "b45bae58-9882-59d5-9b7a-c988374c5c88" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337082 1034 "160" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337082 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535199 true] [17592186337082 1111 #uuid "8b2f192f-2748-5265-96d7-cd12fd7aacfe" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337083 1034 "96" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337083 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535199 true] [17592186337083 1111 #uuid "b2da7c29-cefe-5090-81c6-f5dd571a32f2" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337084 1017 #edb/ref 17592186337085 13194139535199 true] [17592186337084 1089 "q-130771" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337084 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535199 true] [17592186337084 1100 "Suppose $B$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(B)=-75.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{4}{5}{R}_{2}$ and ${R}_{5}↔{R}_{6}.$ What is the value of $det(C)?$" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337084 1113 #uuid "f84f51ef-7655-5ddd-814b-3221e5dd4c7b" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337084 1145 "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{5}↔{R}_{6}$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{4}{5}{R}_{2}$ involves multiplying a row by $\\frac{4}{5},$ so the determinant is multiplied by $\\frac{4}{5}$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one and multiply by $\\frac{4}{5}$ as well. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot (-det(B)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}det(B) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot (-75) \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337085 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337086 13194139535199 true] [17592186337085 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337087 13194139535199 true] [17592186337085 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337088 13194139535199 true] [17592186337085 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337089 13194139535199 true] [17592186337085 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337090 13194139535199 true] [17592186337085 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535199 true] [17592186337085 1041 "selection" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337085 1104 #edb/ref 17592186337086 13194139535199 true] [17592186337085 1110 #uuid "ef923b97-f042-51db-894b-b3bdccf2e667" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337086 1034 "60" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337086 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535199 true] [17592186337086 1111 #uuid "7f2324e3-8eea-513b-84cb-8b138002693e" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337087 1034 "40" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337087 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535199 true] [17592186337087 1111 #uuid "f268ffaf-758c-541d-a3af-ed74bd78a24e" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337088 1034 "-75" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337088 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535199 true] [17592186337088 1111 #uuid "afb71e20-5159-5ba5-aaff-5a081cb43436" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337089 1034 "-90" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337089 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535199 true] [17592186337089 1111 #uuid "fe8d28ab-d8e0-54f1-ae2f-41748d5803c1" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337090 1034 "90" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337090 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535199 true] [17592186337090 1111 #uuid "e3f7ce9a-2702-5c4a-adc7-2cb51679018c" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337091 1017 #edb/ref 17592186337092 13194139535199 true] [17592186337091 1089 "q-130855" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337091 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535199 true] [17592186337091 1100 "Consider the matrices given below. Given that $X$ and $Y$ are row equivalent matrices and $det(X)=5$, find $det(Y).$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,Y=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337091 1113 #uuid "2147c852-ca7d-56cf-bfc5-b94dd52d4711" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337091 1145 "Notice that $Y$ can be obtained from $X$ by swapping the $2$nd and the $3$rd rows. \n\nThis changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =-det(X) \\\\  & =-(5) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337092 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337093 13194139535199 true] [17592186337092 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337094 13194139535199 true] [17592186337092 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337095 13194139535199 true] [17592186337092 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337096 13194139535199 true] [17592186337092 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337097 13194139535199 true] [17592186337092 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535199 true] [17592186337092 1041 "selection" 13194139535199 true] [17592186337092 1104 #edb/ref 17592186337094 13194139535199 true] [1759218633